    <item>
      <title><![CDATA[Your WordPress content, in ZeroPress]]></title>
      <link>https://wordpress.example/try-your-export/</link>
      <dc:creator><![CDATA[editor]]></dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This sample site was built from a WordPress WXR export using the Blog theme. Browse the categories, open a nested menu, or search for a phrase before bringing your own writing.</p>
<h2>Try it with your own posts</h2><ol><li>In WordPress, open <strong>Tools → Export</strong> and choose <strong>All content</strong>.</li><li>Replace <code>wordpress-export.xml</code> in your repository with the downloaded file.</li><li>Commit and push. Cloudflare builds your new site automatically.</li></ol>
<h2>What comes across</h2><table><thead><tr><th>In WordPress</th><th>On this site</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published posts and pages</td><td>Readable articles in the Blog layout</td></tr><tr><td>Categories and tags</td><td>Browseable lists and sidebar links</td></tr><tr><td>Navigation menus</td><td>Up to three levels in the header</td></tr><tr><td>Images and open comments</td><td>Still connected to WordPress</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Your published posts and pages will replace these examples on the next build. The site's title, description, language, and authors come from your export.</p>]]></content:encoded>
      <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Replace one XML file to see your WordPress posts in the Blog theme.]]></excerpt:encoded>
