    <item>
      <title><![CDATA[A notebook for the everyday]]></title>
      <link>https://wordpress.example/everyday-notebook/</link>
      <dc:creator><![CDATA[writer]]></dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I used to wait for a complete idea before opening a notebook. Now I start with a sentence: the bus was late, the rain stopped, someone left a book on the kitchen table.</p><h2>Leave room for the unfinished</h2><p>A note can be useful without becoming an essay. Returning to it a week later is sometimes the only editing it needs.</p><blockquote><p>Write down what you noticed, before deciding what it means.</p></blockquote><h2>A small routine</h2><ul><li>Write the date.</li><li>Keep one concrete detail.</li><li>Stop when there is nothing more to say.</li></ul><p>Over time, these small entries become a record of what held your attention.</p>]]></content:encoded>
      <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Keeping a few ordinary observations is often enough to begin.]]></excerpt:encoded>
