    <item>
      <title><![CDATA[Notes on typography]]></title>
      <link>https://wordpress.example/notes-on-typography/</link>
      <dc:creator><![CDATA[editor]]></dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A comfortable reading page depends on a few quiet decisions. The type does not have to call attention to itself.</p><figure class="wp-block-image"><img src="/demo/type-study.svg" alt="A study of letterforms and type scales" width="960" height="600"><figcaption>Serif headings and a simple body face, shown in a bundled illustration.</figcaption></figure><h2>Give the text room</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>A useful starting point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Body text</td><td>A comfortable size and generous line height</td></tr><tr><td>Paragraphs</td><td>Enough space to see where an idea ends</td></tr><tr><td>Headings</td><td>A clear hierarchy without too many sizes</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Try one change at a time</h2><pre><code class="language-css">.reading-note {
  max-width: 65ch;
  line-height: 1.7;
}</code></pre><p>Read a whole paragraph after every adjustment. A specimen of three words rarely tells the full story.</p>]]></content:encoded>
      <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Line length, rhythm, and a little space around the words.]]></excerpt:encoded>
