    <item>
      <title><![CDATA[A walk before writing]]></title>
      <link>https://wordpress.example/walk-before-writing/</link>
      <dc:creator><![CDATA[writer]]></dc:creator>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>There is a familiar route around the park: past the locked gate, under the plane trees, and back along the water. It takes twenty minutes if I keep moving.</p><h2>A change of pace</h2><p>I went out thinking about a paragraph that would not settle. By the time I reached the bridge, I was thinking about the sound of a bicycle on the boards.</p><blockquote><p>The work was still waiting when I got back. It looked smaller.</p></blockquote><h2>Start with what remains</h2><p>I deleted the first sentence and kept the second. Sometimes that is the whole benefit of a walk.</p>]]></content:encoded>
      <excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[The sentence arrived halfway home, when I had stopped looking for it.]]></excerpt:encoded>
